# Geruest Framework Conventions

## Namespace
All framework code lives in `namespace geruest`. Use `using namespace geruest;` in `.cpp` files only — never in headers.

## Header Guards
```cpp
#ifndef GERUEST_CLASSNAME_HPP
#define GERUEST_CLASSNAME_HPP
// ...
#endif  // GERUEST_CLASSNAME_HPP
```

## Cross-Platform Sockets
Always guard socket types and cleanup with `#ifdef _WIN32`:
```cpp
#ifdef _WIN32
    SOCKET server_fd = INVALID_SOCKET;
    // Use closesocket(), WSACleanup()
#else
    int server_fd = -1;
    // Use close()
#endif
```

## Route Handler Signature
```cpp
using RouteHandler = std::function<HTTPResponse(const HTTPRequest&)>;

server->addRoute("/api/data", [](const HTTPRequest& req) {
    HTTPResponse res("200 OK");
    res.setHeader("Content-Type", "application/json");
    res.setBody(R"({"ok":true})");
    return res;
});
```

## Logging
```cpp
sendToLogger("Info message");        // General info / debug
sendToLoggerError("Error message");  // Errors and warnings
```

## Memory & Performance
- Prefer `std::move` for large strings/responses
- `ServerData` is read-only after `init()` — no locking needed for reads
- Route handlers must be stateless
